				"text": "Whisk masa harina with a little liquid, stir in and simmer to thicken. Finish with vinegar and salt.",
				"uses": [
					"s4",
					"i12",
					"i13"
				],
				"technique": [
					"thicken",
					"simmer"
				],
				"durationMin": 10,
				"heat": "low"
			}
		],
		"notes": {
			"techniques": "Whole dried chiles make the base instead of chili powder, and cubed chuck is braised until it falls apart. Masa harina thickens it and adds a corn flavour.",
			"chemistry": "Collagen in chuck slowly converts to gelatin above about 70 °C during the long simmer, which makes the meat tender and the sauce silky.",
